{
  "$comment": "The gate registry: the steps pnpm validate runs, in order (scripts/validate.mjs). A step runs the root package.json script its id names, as pnpm <id>, unless it carries a command. capability is the owner whose prune removes the step: core, never pruned, or a capability of template.manifest.json; an absent capability takes every step it owns. stage is preflight, workspace or repository, run in that order. profile is the lowest quality profile that runs the step: standard, or strict only. cost is what one run takes: instant, seconds or minutes. blind, exported-cases, marks the one step that blinds a gate: scripts/validate.test.mjs re-runs the exported CASES of its companion against blindGate, and they must fail. Every root script named verify:* or *:test is a step, or an entry of outside, which names the script, the capability whose prune removes the entry and the reason pnpm validate does not run it. Removing a step removes a gate, so this contract is a rule file the write guard asks about. See docs/harness.md section 3.",
